lue then it is rough. Since Fiona is not rough (point 16), she cannot be round and blue.\n- From point 12, we know all blue things are rough. Since Fiona is not rough (point 16), she cannot be blue.\n- From point 13, we know round things are green. Since Anne is round (point 10), she must be green.\n- From point 14, we know all nice things are blue. Since Fiona is not nice (point 5), she cannot be blue.\n- From point 15, we know all rough, nice things are blue. Since Fiona is not nice (point 5), she cannot be blue.\n- From point 16, we know rough, nice things are quiet. Since Fiona is not nice (point 5), she cannot be quiet.\n\nGiven these deductions, we can conclude that Anne is not nice because she is not blue (point 14 and point 15). Therefore, the statement "Anne is nice" is false.\n\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
