ship with itself.\n9. **The tiger is young.** This tells us that the tiger has a positive relationship with being young.\n10. **The tiger is nice.** This tells us that the tiger has a positive relationship with being nice.\n11. **The tiger is young.** This tells us that the tiger has a positive relationship with being young.\n12. **The tiger likes the cat.** This tells us that the tiger has a positive relationship with the cat.\n13. **All big things are blue.** This tells us that if something is big, it is blue.\n14. **If the cat sees the tiger then the cat chases the tiger.** This tells us that if the cat sees the tiger, it will chase the tiger.\n15. **If something likes the rabbit then the rabbit does not like the mouse.** This tells us that if something likes the rabbit, the rabbit will not like the mouse.\n16. **All blue things are young.** This tells us that if something is blue, it is young.\n17. **If something is blue then it is young.** This tells us that if something is blue, it is young.\n18. **If something chases the cat then it likes the mouse.** This tells us that if something chases the cat, it will like the mouse.\n19. **If something is young then it likes the tiger.** This tells us that if something is young, it will like the tiger.\n20. **If something likes the mouse then the mouse is big.** This tells us that if something likes the mouse, the mouse will be big.\n21. **If something sees the mouse and the mouse is not blue then the mouse likes the cat.** This tells us that if something sees the mouse and the mouse is not blue, the mouse will like the cat.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the question: "Based on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? The mouse is young."\n\nFrom the information provided, we know that:\n- The tiger is young.\n- If something sees the mouse and the mouse is not blue, the mouse likes the cat.\n- If something is young, it likes the tiger.\n- If something likes the mouse, the mouse is big.\n\nSince